)_-_0.5rem)]"}><span className={"custom-figure text-[2.25rem] text-primary-ink"}>{"10 min"}</span><span className={"text-base text-soft"}>{"of brisk walking, twice a day"}</span></div></div><figcaption>{"Rough guides for healthy adults. Your doctor may set a different goal."}</figcaption></figure><h2 id={"mc-ar-start"}>{"Start from where you are"}</h2><p>{"Look at your average over the last week, not your best day. Add about a thousand steps a day, keep that for two weeks, then add another thousand. Small and steady beats a burst that hurts your knees."}</p><ul><li>{"Walk the first or last ten minutes of your commute."}</li><li>{"Take phone calls on your feet."}</li><li>{"After dinner, a short walk round the block helps blood sugar too."}</li></ul><h2 id={"mc-ar-when"}>{"When to talk to us first"}</h2><p>{"If you have a heart condition, have had chest pain on exertion, or get unusually short of breath, check with your doctor before you increase your activity. A quick ECG or a stress test can tell us what is safe."}</p><blockquote>{"“Walking is the medicine I prescribe most. It is cheap, it has almost no side effects, and it works.”"}<cite>{"Dr. Ryan Mitchell, MD, Cardiology"}</cite></blockquote><p className={"flex items-start gap-3 p-5 text-base font-semibold text-text bg-(--custom-tint) rounded-lg"}><i className={"ph ph-warning-circle text-xl text-primary-ink"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i><span>{"Chest pain, pressure or tightness during a walk is not something to push through. Stop and call 911."}</span></p><p className={"text-base text-(--custom-meta)"}>{"This article is general information, not a substitute for advice from your own doctor. Individual results vary."}</p></article><aside className={"grid gap-6 lg:sticky lg:top-[calc(var(--navbar-h,88px)_+_2rem)]"} aria-label={"About this article"}><a href={"#page=demo-medical-clinic-1-doctor"} className={"custom-quick border border-(--custom-line)"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/720x